"""Build a dependency-free, evidence-linked executive summary."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
from html import escape
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
HIST=[(24,'h25-1-dotted-h19-5-d1-5-20261002-989f59505db1-nan','0.2477'),(25,'dotted-h19-5-d2-8-20261002-e56ea318af89-nan','0.2600'),(27,'topo-gap-closure-t-v2-on-d1-5-20261002-5512495c6bd1-nan','0.2449'),(28,'h36-1-rung30-blind-r1-20261003-b531dae0a36f-nan','0.2710'),(30,'d28-poisson300m-offcat-44090-20261003T233156Z-91eae1ca','0.2600'),(31,'h27-4-solo-d28-20261004-8acb75e1-nan','0.2708'),(32,'h33-h33-2-b2-20261004T220000Z-e5eb6e7e-zeros','0.2778'),(33,'h33d-analog-tip-stepover-r30-20261004-cb490425926e','0.2632'),(36,'anderson-geothermal-pinn-38854-20261004T230000Z-9b9ea4e6-zeros','0.2750')]
CSS='''body{font:17px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;background:#f4f7fa;color:#172d3c;margin:0}main{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:36px 24px}nav{display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap}a{color:#075a89}h1{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,48px);line-height:1.1}section,.notice{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd7df;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:24px 0}.notice{border-left:6px solid #aa3525;background:#fff4ee}.badge{font-weight:bold;color:#983122}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}th,td{padding:14px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd6de}th{background:#e6eef3}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere} .scroll{overflow-x:auto}footer{font-size:14px}'''
def page(title,body):
 return f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{escape(title)}</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head><body><main><nav><a href="index.html">Executive summary</a><a href="submission.html">Submission guide</a><a href="research.md">Research plan</a><a href="evidence/index.json">Evidence manifest</a><a href="run-card.json">Run card</a></nav>{body}<footer>Audit date: 26 October 2026 · Repository snapshots are third-party evidence, not organizer receipts. No competition slot used.</footer></main></body></html>'
rows=[]
manifest=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/evidence/index.json').read_text())
for n,name,reported in HIST:
 commit=next(r['commit'] for r in manifest['repositories'] if r['site']==n)
 source='README.md' if (ROOT/f'docs/evidence/GEMSDOE{n}/README.md').exists() else 'docs/index.html'
 url=f'https://github.com/buffedlizard55-lab/GEMSDOE{n}/blob/{commit}/{source}'
 rows.append(f'<tr><td><a href="{url}">GEMSDOE{n}</a><br><small>snapshot {commit[:8]}</small></td><td><code>{escape(name)}</code><br>Owner-reported historical result: {reported}; NOT ORGANIZER-CONFIRMED</td><td>None approved</td><td>Unavailable — no HOLDOUT-DTI measured here</td><td>Not verified; historic file is not a new submission</td><td class="badge">DO NOT SUBMIT</td></tr>')
body='''<p>GEMS · Scientific submission audit</p><h1>Evidence first.<br>No untested submission.</h1><div class="notice"><strong>NO APPROVED TIFF TO DOWNLOAD OR SUBMIT.</strong><p>This checkout contains commit-pinned third-party source snapshots, but no competition raster data, local feature cache, complete current registry, or runnable shared-template experiment. No new experiment or raster was generated. The assigned method lane is unspecified. Blocking submission is intentional—not a request for human raster inspection.</p></div><section><h2>Decision at a glance</h2><p>GEMSDOE32 has the highest historical owner-reported result among the nine requested sites (0.2778 OWNER-REPORTED in the supplied record; no receipt-to-raster-hash link found in the pinned source snapshot). It is not a new candidate. No evidence in this checkout establishes a unique new submission that beats a current same-evaluator holdout best. No projected leaderboard score is defensible.</p><p>The official public leaderboard page displayed 0.4437 for its first entry when retrieved on 2026-10-26 UTC. This dated public-page snapshot is not a private/final score or a receipt for any file in this repo. The prompt's 0.3195 and 0.4413 values are older/conflicting snapshots. Recheck the official page before any decision.</p></section><section><h2>Nine-site executive table</h2><p>Each row identifies the historical best supplied in the request, not a recommendation to resubmit it. Links point to commit-pinned repository documentation. No authenticated organizer receipt was obtained.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Site / source</th><th>Historical artifact / evidence class</th><th>File to download</th><th>Estimated score</th><th>Unique across registry?</th><th>Decision</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(rows)+'''</tbody></table></div></section><section><h2>Why the dotted champion may work</h2><p>The pinned GEMSDOE32 source snapshot describes H33-2-B2 as a dotted ridge-derived mask, with catalogue-near dots pruned. The official DTI gives false negatives four times the alpha-weighted false-positive coefficient (beta 0.8 vs alpha 0.2) and triangular distance credit within 300 m. A sparse, spatially broad ridge mask can plausibly retain credit around hidden faults while limiting false-positive prediction mass; pruning around known faults may reduce direct dependence on the catalogue. Pinned site records describe a nested H19-5 → D2.8 → B1 → B2 family, with dots pruned near mapped faults; the historical scores remain owner-reported claims. The mechanism is plausible because low-marginal-credit dots near known traces may be removed while preserving distance-kernel coverage elsewhere, but only the exact scored TIFF and hidden labels could establish causation. Also, the `h33-h33-2-b2` filename does not by itself prove it came from the later H33-A..E experimental module in the archived source tree. See the detailed audit in the project README and the source irregularity log. No higher leaderboard score can be inferred from this chain alone.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/buffedlizard55-lab/GEMSDOE32/blob/07806249f4ed3efe70b4fbf866183c32392b7853/README.md">Pinned GEMSDOE32 source snapshot</a> · <a href="evidence/GEMSDOE32/evidence/h33_holdout.json">archived local holdout record (not rerun here)</a> · <a href="https://github.com/kanlerxz87-cyber/KANLERGEMSDOE2/blob/main/README.md">Full nine-site metric and lineage review</a> · <a href="research.md">Ranked four-hypothesis plan and limitations →</a> · <a href="research/source-audit.md">Source irregularity audit →</a></p></section><section><h2>Non-negotiable automated gates</h2><ol><li>Assigned lane and complete registry; surface and final-dot duplication checks.</li><li>Per-feature leakage canaries and buffered, segment-level, visible-only holdout.</li><li>Versioned HOLDOUT-DTI, withheld positives and paired improvement confidence interval.</li><li>Canonical writer plus finite [0,1] predictions, single band, exact CRS, shape and transform.</li><li>Separate selector and authenticated weekly-cap check. Passing format is not approval.</li></ol><p>Literal lattice overlap is a reported blocker in GEMSDOE32. We do not exempt it or perturb an old raster to manufacture uniqueness.</p></section><section><h2>Sources and next actions</h2><p><a href="evidence/official-reference-README.md">Official reference README snapshot</a> · <a href="https://github.com/drivendataorg/gems-prize-reference-solution">Organizer reference implementation</a> · <a href="https://www.drivendata.org/competitions/306/competition-doe-gems/leaderboard/">Official public leaderboard (snapshot reviewed 2026-10-26)</a> · <a href="https://www.drivendata.org/competitions/306/competition-doe-gems/page/967/">Official metric/submission specification</a></p><p>Next session: recover the shared template/cache from a verified source; resolve the lane and literal-registry conflict; verify semantic band mapping; freeze folds and current best; run at most three experiments. No claims that training requires a GPU: the official reference supports CPU training, albeit slower.</p></section>'''
(ROOT/'docs/index.html').write_text(page('GEMS executive summary',body))
(ROOT/'docs/style.css').write_text(CSS)
(ROOT/'docs/submission.html').write_text(page('GEMS submission guide','''<h1>How to submit—only after approval</h1><div class="notice"><strong>Current status: BLOCKED. There is no approved file.</strong></div><section><h2>1. Generate and validate</h2><p>Reuse the selected template’s canonical submission_writer.py. Validate the reopened final bytes against the organizer sample: single-band float32 GeoTIFF, exact CRS/shape/geotransform, finite predictions in the sample-template footprint and values in [0,1], with null/nodata outside the footprint. Run the repository checker with <code>python scripts/validate_submission.py --template data/sample_submission.tif --candidate candidate.tif --json candidate-audit.json</code> after installing <code>requirements-validation.txt</code>. It validates format only; it does not approve a submission. Never blindly clip an invalid model output to hide a bug.</p><h2>2. Verify scientific eligibility</h2><p>Require feature-alone canaries, buffered whole-segment fold-local evaluation, positive paired improvement confidence interval and complete surface/dot uniqueness checks. Record SHA256, unique submission name and a note no longer than 140 characters.</p><h2>3. Separate selector</h2><p>Promotion means eligible for selection, not authorized upload. Check the authenticated weekly cap and current rules before spending a slot. This project has made no submissions.</p><h2>4. Upload the approved artifact</h2><p>At the <a href="https://www.drivendata.org/competitions/306/competition-doe-gems/">official competition</a>, use New submission. Upload the approved .tif or a .zip containing just that GeoTIFF, and copy its manifest note. Preserve the organizer receipt tied to the exact final raster hash. Only receipt results may be labeled ORGANIZER-CONFIRMED.</p><h2>Range-error diagnosis</h2><p>“Predicted values must be in range [0, 1]” requires checking every output value and nodata metadata. Negative sentinels, infinities and unbounded model outputs are possible causes; the specific failed file was not provided, so its cause is unknown.</p></section>'''))
